The error is caused by the first use of `l_batch`:

```text
l_batch.EXTEND;
```

In the supplied function, `l_batch` is declared as a nested table:

```text
TYPE batch_t IS TABLE OF NUMBER;
l_batch batch_t;
```

but it is never initialized. A PL/SQL collection variable of this kind starts out null/uninitialized, so calling `EXTEND` on it raises:

```text
ORA-06531: Reference to uninitialized collection
```

The minimal repair is to initialize the nested table before it is extended. The complete replacement unit is:

```plsql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION first_batch RETURN NUMBER IS
  TYPE batch_t IS TABLE OF NUMBER;
  l_batch batch_t := batch_t();
BEGIN
  l_batch.EXTEND;
  l_batch(1) := 17;
  RETURN l_batch(1);
END first_batch;
```

What changed: only the declaration of `l_batch` was changed from an uninitialized collection variable to one initialized with the empty nested table constructor `batch_t()`. The rest of the function is left as supplied. I have not compiled or run this replacement.

