DECLARE
  l_failures PLS_INTEGER := 0;

  PROCEDURE check_clamp_nonnegative(
    p_check_name VARCHAR2,
    p_input      NUMBER,
    p_expected   NUMBER
  ) IS
    l_actual NUMBER;
  BEGIN
    l_actual := HARNESS_APP.clamp_nonnegative(p_input);

    IF (l_actual = p_expected) OR (l_actual IS NULL AND p_expected IS NULL) THEN
      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
        'PASS: ' || p_check_name ||
        ', input=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(p_input), 'NULL') ||
        ', expected=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(p_expected), 'NULL') ||
        ', actual=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(l_actual), 'NULL')
      );
    ELSE
      l_failures := l_failures + 1;
      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
        'FAIL: ' || p_check_name ||
        ', input=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(p_input), 'NULL') ||
        ', expected=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(p_expected), 'NULL') ||
        ', actual=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(l_actual), 'NULL')
      );
    END IF;
  EXCEPTION
    WHEN OTHERS THEN
      l_failures := l_failures + 1;
      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
        'FAIL: ' || p_check_name ||
        ', input=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(p_input), 'NULL') ||
        ', expected=' || COALESCE(TO_CHAR(p_expected), 'NULL') ||
        ', raised=' || SQLERRM
      );
  END check_clamp_nonnegative;
BEGIN
  SAVEPOINT before_clamp_nonnegative_test;

  check_clamp_nonnegative('NULL input', NULL, NULL);
  check_clamp_nonnegative('negative input', -1, 0);
  check_clamp_nonnegative('zero input', 0, 0);
  check_clamp_nonnegative('positive input', 42, 42);

  IF l_failures = 0 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Summary: 0 failure(s)');
  ELSE
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Summary: ' || l_failures || ' failure(s)');
  END IF;

  ROLLBACK TO before_clamp_nonnegative_test;

  IF l_failures <> 0 THEN
    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20999, 'clamp_nonnegative test failed with ' || l_failures || ' failure(s)');
  END IF;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error: ' || SQLERRM);
    ROLLBACK TO before_clamp_nonnegative_test;
    RAISE;
END;
```

The block calls the stored function by name, `HARNESS_APP.clamp_nonnegative`, rather than copying its code into the test. It checks four cases:

- `NULL` input: expects `NULL`, because the selected function’s `CASE` condition is unknown for `NULL` and the `ELSE` branch returns the input value.
- negative input: expects `0`.
- zero input: expects `0`.
- positive input: expects the same positive value.

Each check prints either `PASS` or `FAIL`, including the expected and actual values. If a call raises an unexpected error, that check also prints `FAIL` and counts as a failure. The block uses a savepoint and rolls back to it before finishing, so it does not commit any work. If any check fails, it raises an application error after the rollback. I have not run or compiled this block.

